Done. Here's what changed in the `rust/` crate:

**`src/lib.rs`** — added `filter_by_tag`:
```rust
pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes
        .iter()
        .filter(|n| n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag))
        .collect()
}
```
Exact match via `==` (not substring), returns `&Note` refs in original order.

**`src/main.rs`** — `list` command now parses a `--tag <TAG>` flag, errors out if the flag is present without an argument, and routes through `filter_by_tag` when given (falls back to all notes otherwise). Added `Note` to the crate import.

**`tests/basic.rs`** — two tests: exact-match-only (a `#rustic` tag is excluded when filtering `rust`) and order preservation / empty result for no match.

